# Semantic Communication System - Complete Architecture & Split of Work

This document outlines the detailed system structure, modules, packet design, database schema, and split of work across phases for our local, low-resource semantic communication prototype.

---

## 1. System Structure (Files & Modules)

```
semantic-communication/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── main.py          # API Endpoints (POST /encode, POST /decode, POST /validate, GET /history, GET /)
│   ├── extractor.py     # Semantic extraction logic (Normal vs Low-Resource)
│   ├── encoder.py       # Compact packet serializer (UTF-8 bytes, key mapping)
│   ├── decoder.py       # Reconstructs natural language from packet keys
│   ├── validator.py     # Semantic comparison engine (SAFE, REVIEW_REQUIRED, FAILED)
│   └── database.py      # SQLite connection & queries (storing communication workflows)
├── tests/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── test_semantic.py # Automated test cases (pytest)
├── data/
│   └── semantic.db      # Local SQLite database (git-ignored)
├── requirements.txt
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

